[b]Den Designer[/b] lets you decorate the Den from inside the game. Add props from a searchable catalog, rearrange existing scenery, and build anything from a small desk display to a complete room layout.

Walk up to the office console and choose [b]OPEN DEN DESIGNER[/b], or press [b]Ctrl+Home[/b] anywhere in the Den. Fly around, move things into place, and save your work. Decorations use the mod's own saves, separately from your campaign saves.

[b]Runs entirely as a pak mod. No UE4SS or additional runtime DLL is required.[/b]

[heading]Features[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]A catalog of thousands of game props[/b]: search, collections, recently used props and generated thumbnail cards.[/*]
[*][b]Rearrange existing scenery[/b]: move, rotate, resize, duplicate or store eligible props already in the Den.[/*]
[*][b]A flying editor camera[/b]: move around your work, look with the mouse and frame the selected prop.[/*]
[*][b]Several ways to edit[/b]: surface dragging, height dragging, axis/plane gizmos, numeric fields and keyboard nudges.[/*]
[*][b]Grid and nearby-prop snapping[/b]: line up edges and centres, fit objects flush against each other, or stack them. Guide lines show the match; hold Alt to bypass nearby-prop snapping.[/*]
[*][b]A choice of rotation pivots[/b]: turn props around their centre, bottom, top or original mesh origin.[/*]
[*][b]Independent selection filters[/b]: Floors, Walls and Structure, plus adjustable selection range.[/*]
[*][b]Undo/redo and a Storeroom[/b]: undo edits, keep props out of the way, and restore stored items later.[/*]
[*][b]Shared and campaign-specific layouts[/b]: decorate once for your campaigns, or give a particular campaign its own look. Named presets let you keep different full-layout designs.[/*]
[*][b]Reusable compositions[/b]: save groups of up to 128 props, browse pictures of the whole arrangement and place more copies across campaigns.[/*]
[*][b]Independent prop-pack support[/b]: compatible packs add their own catalog shelves and work with placement, the Storeroom and compositions.[/*]
[*][b]Draft recovery and rotating backups[/b]: recover unfinished work after an interrupted editing session.[/*]
[*][b]In-game settings and rebindable keys[/b]: tune the camera, snapping, rotation pivot, background tasks and editor controls. Help shows your active bindings.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Using Den Designer[/heading]
Enter the Den, then use the [b]office console[/b] marked with a pencil icon or press [b]Ctrl+Home[/b]. The game's HUD hides while you edit and returns when you finish.

[b]Camera and selection[/b]
[list]
[*][b]WASD[/b] flies, [b]Space[/b] rises and [b]Ctrl[/b] descends. Hold [b]right mouse[/b] to look and [b]Shift[/b] to fly faster.[/*]
[*][b]Left-click[/b] selects a prop. [b]F[/b] frames it in the camera.[/*]
[*]Choose [b]Select, Move, Rotate or Scale[/b] on the menu bar, or press [b]T[/b] to cycle them.[/*]
[*][b]Floors, Walls and Structure[/b] independently allow selection of those pieces. Range sets how far away you can select.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Placing and editing[/b]
[list]
[*]Open [b]Catalog[/b], choose a prop and click in the world to place it. [b]Shift-click[/b] places more copies; [b]Esc[/b] cancels placement.[/*]
[*]Drag a selected prop along a surface, or hold [b]Shift[/b] while dragging to change its height.[/*]
[*][b]Q/E[/b] or the [b]mouse wheel[/b] turns it. [b]Shift+wheel[/b] makes fine turns. [b]+/−[/b], including the keypad keys, scales it.[/*]
[*]Use the gizmo handles to constrain an edit, or type precise position, rotation and scale values in the inspector and press [b]Enter[/b].[/*]
[*][b]Arrow keys[/b] nudge horizontally; [b]Page Up/Down[/b] nudge vertically.[/*]
[*][b]C[/b] copies, [b]X[/b] or [b]Delete[/b] stores, and [b]Z/Y[/b] undo/redo. Stored props can be restored from the [b]Storeroom[/b].[/*]
[*][b]R[/b] resets an existing scenery edit. On a placed prop it straightens pitch/roll and resets scale, keeping its yaw.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Snapping and pivots[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Grid[/b] or [b]G[/b] cycles Off, 5, 10, 25 and 50 cm steps.[/*]
[*][b]Snap[/b] matches nearby props: flush faces, aligned edges/centres and stacked objects. Hold [b]Alt[/b] to bypass this while moving; the grid remains independent.[/*]
[*]Change [b]Pivot[/b] beside the rotation fields to Centre, Bottom, Top or Original. Numeric, gizmo and wheel/key rotation all use that point.[/*]
[/list]

Choose [b]Save[/b] to commit the layout and [b]Done[/b] to return to the game. Closing with unsaved work offers Save, Discard or Keep editing. The opening shortcut also requests exit.
These are the default controls. If you rebind fast flight, the new key also controls fine wheel turns and height dragging.

[heading]Layouts, Presets and Compositions[/heading]
[b]Home[/b] is shared by campaigns that do not have their own layout. In [b]Layouts[/b], give the current campaign its own copy, switch it back to Home, or save/load named presets of a complete layout. The selected saved layout applies when the Den loads and on return from missions.

[b]Compositions[/b] are reusable groups rather than full-layout replacements. Choose [b]Select parts[/b], click props to include them, finish selecting, name the arrangement and save it. Select its thumbnail and choose [b]Place selected[/b] to put down another copy. Each placement is one undo step, and its parts can then be edited individually.

Compositions preserve relative transforms and supported material overrides, with a bottom-centre placement anchor. They are available across campaigns and their library saves immediately. Replacing or deleting a saved composition leaves previously placed copies in your layout.

[heading]Settings[/heading]
Open [b]Settings[/b] in the editor to adjust:
[list]
[*]Flight speed, fast-flight multiplier and mouse-look sensitivity.[/*]
[*]Nearby-prop snapping, its guides and close-up snap distance (2–30 cm; default 8 cm).[/*]
[*]The rotation pivot.[/*]
[*]Draft autosave and thumbnail generation.[/*]
[*]The editor opening shortcut and supported keyboard bindings.[/*]
[/list]
Settings save automatically and apply immediately. Reset settings restores defaults. Mouse controls, Alt's nearby-snap bypass, Esc, Delete, arrows, Page Up/Down and +/− remain fixed. F9 is reserved.

[heading]Prop Packs[/heading]
Compatible prop packs add static meshes under [b]Catalog → All collections → Prop packs[/b]. Each pack gets its own shelf; its name, author and tags also work in search.

Install all three matching containers from a pack while the game is closed, then restart. Removing a pack keeps its entries in your layouts, so reinstalling it at the same asset paths lets its meshes resolve again.

Prop packs and creator tools are separate from the runtime. [b]The runtime download contains no sample pack or model importer.[/b] Creator documentation is in the source repository; the separate editor tools remain a preview pending Windows editor testing.

[heading]Requirements[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Star Wars: Zero Company[/b][/*]
[*][b]Keyboard and mouse[/b] for the editor.[/*]
[/list]
The current runtime targets the Steam release, build [b]25898267[/b]. Other game builds and the EA App release are unverified.
UE4SS and a separate mod-settings manager are not required. Keep UE4SS installed if your other mods need it.

[heading]Installation[/heading]
[b]Mod manager[/b]
Install the downloaded ZIP through your mod manager and enable [b]Den Designer[/b]. The archive includes metadata for the community managers:
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/29]Zero Mod Manager[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/121]Zero Company Mod Command[/url][/*]
[/list]
The runtime is one component. Install all three of its container files from the same version.

[b]Manual installation[/b]
Close the game, then extract the ZIP into the game's [b]SWZeroCompany[/b] folder, the one containing [b]Binaries[/b] and [b]Content[/b], and merge folders. The installed files should include:
[code]SWZeroCompany/Content/Paks/~mods/DenDesigner/DenDesignerGF_P.pak
SWZeroCompany/Content/Paks/~mods/DenDesigner/DenDesignerGF_P.ucas
SWZeroCompany/Content/Paks/~mods/DenDesigner/DenDesignerGF_P.utoc[/code]
Keep the accompanying metadata and player guide in that folder too.

[b]Updating[/b]
Close the game and update through the same manager, or replace the DenDesigner folder for a manual install. Keep your mod data. If upgrading from an older flat installation, remove its old [b]DenDesignerGF_P.pak[/b], [b].ucas[/b] and [b].utoc[/b] directly inside [b]Content/Paks/~mods[/b]. Do not leave duplicate copies for the game to load; keep backups outside the Paks folders.

[b]Uninstalling[/b]
Close the game and remove Den Designer through your manager, or delete [b]Content/Paks/~mods/DenDesigner[/b]. The mod's decorations stop applying and your campaign saves remain usable. Keep its saved data if you may reinstall.

[heading]Saved Data and Recovery[/heading]
Layouts, presets, compositions and settings live in the mod's own save directory:
[code]%LOCALAPPDATA%\SWZeroCompany\Saved\SaveGames\ZComDen\Native\v1[/code]
Back up [b]the whole directory[/b] together; do not mix individual rotating banks from different backups. Thumbnail images are cached separately under [b]Saved/ZComDen/thumbs[/b] and can be regenerated.

Draft autosave is on by default. After an interrupted session, opening the editor offers recovery; a draft does not silently replace the saved layout. Use [b]Save[/b] to commit your design.

Edits that cannot currently resolve their objects remain in the layout and appear in the Storeroom's unavailable list. You can keep them for returning content or forget individual entries; Undo can restore a forgotten entry in the active session.

[heading]Compatibility and Limits[/heading]
[list]
[*]Den Designer edits eligible static meshes in the Den. Characters, animated objects, individual instanced-mesh pieces and protected gameplay/interactable objects are outside its supported selection scope.[/*]
[*]Placed meshes are decorations; they do not acquire the original object's scripts or gameplay interactions.[/*]
[*]Compatible prop packs are the supported way to add independent mesh content. Other mods' gameplay objects are not automatically editable.[/*]
[*]Mods or game updates that change Den objects, asset paths or streaming may affect saved edits. Missing entries are retained for review.[/*]
[*]There is no verified compatibility list for every mod combination. Back up your mod data before changing your content setup.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Known Issues[/heading]
[list]
[*]The editor is designed for keyboard and mouse; controller editing is not supported.[/*]
[*]The editor's interface text is in English.[/*]
[*]Thumbnails may take time to appear on first use. Generation can be disabled in Settings.[/*]
[*]A prop-pack update that changes a mesh's appearance can leave an old cached thumbnail. Delete that mesh's cached PNG to regenerate it.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Troubleshooting[/heading]
If something goes wrong, please include:
[list]
[*]Your game build and Den Designer version.[/*]
[*]Your other installed mods and prop packs.[/*]
[*]What you were doing, what happened and any on-screen message.[/*]
[*]A screenshot or short recording where useful.[/*]
[*][b]SWZeroCompany.log[/b] from [b]%LOCALAPPDATA%\SWZeroCompany\Saved\Logs[/b], if the game produced one.[/*]
[/list]
If the console prompt is unavailable, try [b]Ctrl+Home[/b] after the Den has finished loading, or your replacement shortcut. If a keyboard binding causes trouble, check [b]Help[/b] and [b]Settings[/b] for the active bindings and conflicts.
The included player guide covers installation, saved data and recovery. Logs can contain local folder paths; look them over before sharing.

[heading]Source Code and Issue Reports[/heading]
Source, the full feature guide, creator documentation and issue tracking are available on [url=https://github.com/chatterchats/DenDesigner]GitHub[/url]. You can also report problems in the Bugs tab here on Nexus.

